num => 15, slug => 'handling-rejection', module => 4, read => 7, diff => '🟡 Intermediate',
title => 'Handling Rejection and Asking for Feedback', cn => '拒信应对与索取反馈',
focus => 'The two-line reply that keeps the door open and harvests the feedback',
scenario => [
q{The rejection email arrives on a Tuesday morning: <em>"After careful consideration, we have decided to progress with other candidates…"</em> You read it three times. The job you wanted is gone. <strong>What you do in the next twenty minutes decides whether this was a dead end or an expensive lesson with a return address.</strong>},
q{周二早上拒信来了：<em>"经过慎重考虑，我们决定推进其他候选人……"</em>你读了三遍。想要的工作没了。<strong>接下来二十分钟的行动，决定这是一条死路，还是一堂留了回信地址的昂贵课程。</strong>},
q{The professional move has two parts: <strong>a two-line reply that keeps the relationship</strong> — no bargaining, no wounded dignity — and <strong>one precise feedback question</strong> that a busy recruiter can actually answer in one sentence. Then you file it, and you keep running your other loops.},
q{职业化动作有两部分：<strong>两句话的回复保住关系</strong>——不讨价还价、不流露受伤的自尊——以及<strong>一个精确的反馈问题</strong>，忙到飞起的招聘者用一句话就能回答。然后归档，继续跑你的其他流程。},
],
dialogue => [
['You (Candidate)', q{Twenty minutes, two jobs. <strong>Job one: the two-line reply.</strong> Not five lines, not a paragraph — two. <em>"Thank you for letting me know — I appreciate the speed and the direct note. I remain interested in future roles on the team; my door is open."</em> <strong>Cool, professional, zero guilt.</strong>}, q{二十分钟，两件事。<strong>第一件：两句话的回复。</strong>不是五句，不是一段——两句。<em>"感谢告知—— appreciate 你们反馈的迅速与直接。我对团队未来的岗位保持兴趣，我的门是开着的。"</em><strong>冷静、职业、零愧疚。</strong>}],
['You (Candidate)', q{<strong>Job two: the one-question feedback ask.</strong> Not "do you have any feedback?" — that is a homework assignment. One question a recruiter can answer while walking to a meeting: <em>"If you can share one thing — was it domain depth, seniority fit, or something in the interviews themselves?"</em> <strong>Three options make it answerable in five seconds.</strong>}, q{<strong>第二件：一个问题的反馈请求。</strong>不是"有什么反馈吗？"——那是一份作业。要问一个招聘者走向会议室的路上就能回答的问题：<em>"如果能分享一点——是领域深度、资历匹配，还是面试本身的表现？"</em><strong>给出三个选项，五秒内就能回答。</strong>}],
['You (Candidate)', q{And the discipline list. <strong>Do not:</strong> argue the decision, ask which candidate beat me, re-open the interview answers, or send it from an account named after my cat. <strong>Do:</strong> send within one business day, from the same thread, <em>signed the way I would sign any professional email</em>.}, q{然后是纪律清单。<strong>不要：</strong>质疑决定、问我被谁击败、重开面试答案、或者用我家猫的名字注册的邮箱发送。<strong>要：</strong>一个工作日内发出、在原邮件串里回复、<em>用我会签任何一封职业邮件的方式落款</em>。}],
['You (Candidate)', q{What happens next is the part nobody teaches: <strong>file the feedback where decisions happen.</strong> A note in my job-search tracker: <em>"HSBC TL round — feedback: panel felt payments depth strong, mentoring evidence thin — build two coaching stories."</em> <strong>The rejection just became a requirement in my development backlog.</strong>}, q{接下来的环节没人教：<strong>把反馈归档到"做决定的地方"。</strong>求职追踪表里加一条：<em>"汇丰 TL 轮——反馈：小组认为支付深度够，带人证据不足——补两个带人故事。"</em><strong>这封拒信刚刚变成我发展待办清单里的一条需求。</strong>}],
['You (Candidate)', q{Six months later, that same recruiter posts a new QA Lead opening. <strong>Whose name is in her mind?</strong> The candidate who said thank you and meant it. <em>Rejection handled well is the cheapest networking there is.</em>}, q{六个月后，同一位招聘者发布了新的 QA Lead 岗位。<strong>她脑海里会浮现谁的名字？</strong>那个说了谢谢而且是真心的候选人。<em>处理得当的拒信是最便宜的人脉。</em>}],
],
phrases => [
['Receipt', q{Thank you for letting me know — I appreciate the speed and the direct note.}, q{感谢告知—— appreciate 反馈的迅速与直接。}, q{Thanking them for the speed reframes the rejection as professional service — dignity intact.}],
['Door', q{I remain interested in future roles on the team; my door is open.}, q{我对团队未来的岗位保持兴趣；我的门是开着的。}, q{The exact sentence that puts you in the "keep warm" pile for the next req.}],
['Ask', q{Was it domain depth, seniority fit, or the interviews themselves?}, q{是领域深度、资历匹配，还是面试表现？}, q{One question, three menus — answerable in five seconds, useful for a year.}],
['Ban', q{Which candidate beat me?}, q{我被谁击败了？}, q{The question you are entitled to feel and forbidden to send. It burns the relationship it should build.}],
['Convert', q{The rejection just became a requirement in my development backlog.}, q{拒信变成了我发展待办里的一条需求。}, q{The whole mindset in one line: feedback is a ticket, not a verdict.}],
['Long game', q{Rejection handled well is the cheapest networking there is.}, q{处理得当的拒信是最便宜的人脉。}, q{Why the two-line reply matters: recruiters remember the graceful ones when the next role opens.}],
],
