grammar => [
['Present simple for permanent doors', q{<em>"I remain interested in future roles."</em> — present simple, not "I will remain interested". Present simple states a standing fact about you, the way you would describe a permanent feature: <em>"my door is open"</em>. Future tense makes the interest sound conditional on their next move; present tense makes it a property of the candidate.}, q{"I remain interested in future roles."——一般现在时，而不是 "I will remain interested"。现在时陈述的是一个关于你的恒常事实，如同描述一个永久属性："my door is open"。将来时让兴趣听起来取决于对方的下一步；现在时让它成为候选人的固有属性。}],
['Choice questions with three-part menus', q{<em>"Was it domain depth, seniority fit, or the interviews themselves?"</em> — the <strong>A, B, or C</strong> question form does the respondent\'s work in advance. Open questions ("any feedback?") create effort; menu questions create a click. The grammar of kindness in professional email is often just: offer the options.}, q{"Was it domain depth, seniority fit, or the interviews themselves?"——<strong>A、B 还是 C</strong> 问句预先完成了对方的思考工作。开放式问题（"有什么反馈吗？"）制造负担；菜单式问题只需点选。职业邮件里的善意语法，往往就是"把选项摆出来"。}],
],
tips => [
q{<strong>Reply within one business day.</strong> Speed signals composure; the two-liner takes two minutes and outlives the pain.},
q{<strong>Never argue the decision.</strong> There is no version of "you are wrong" that ends with a job offer. The reply is for the next req, not this one.},
q{<strong>One feedback question, menu-shaped.</strong> Busy people answer five-second questions; they archive homework.},
q{<strong>File feedback as a backlog item.</strong> "Mentoring evidence thin — build two coaching stories" is a ticket with a due date, not a wound.},
q{<strong>The same recruiter staffs the next req.</strong> Graceful candidates get remembered at exactly the moment it pays.},
],
practice => [
{ t => 'Write your two-liner', p => 'Draft the two-sentence reply to a real rejection: thanks with one specific appreciation, door left open in present simple.', a => q{The specific appreciation is the craft: "the speed and the direct note", "the panel\'s time on a Friday" — something true about HOW they communicated. Generic thanks read as template; specific thanks read as character.} },
{ t => 'Feedback menu', p => 'Build your three-option feedback question for the role you most recently lost. All three options must be things a recruiter could know.', a => q{Good menus use things the process actually measured: domain depth, seniority fit, interview performance, notice period, salary alignment. "Was my CV typo the reason?" — no: they may not know, and now they do.} },
{ t => 'Backlog conversion', p => 'Take a rejection you have received (or simulate one) and write the tracker line: role, round, feedback hypothesis, one concrete next action.', a => q{Format: "HSBC TL round — hypothesis: mentoring evidence thin. Action: two coaching stories with named engineers and outcomes, by next month." The line must contain a verb you can complete, not a feeling you can nurse.} },
],
