dialogue => [
['Sarah (Hiring Manager)', q{Your CV is an interesting read. <em>Eight years in accounting — why business analysis, and why should I believe it sticks?</em>}, q{你的简历很有意思。<em>做了八年会计——为什么转业务分析？我凭什么相信你不会转回去？</em>}],
['You (Candidate)', q{The honest arc: <strong>I did not leave accounting — I followed the part of it I was good at.</strong> For three of those eight years I was the accountant who ended up in the systems projects: the ERP migration, the close-process redesign. <em>Every time a finance transformation project needed someone who spoke both ledgers and requirements, I was in the room.</em>}, q{真实的弧线是：<strong>我不是离开会计——我是追随了其中我擅长的部分。</strong>八年里有三年，我是那个"总是被卷进系统项目"的会计：ERP 迁移、结账流程重设计。<em>每次财务变革项目需要一个既懂账又懂需求的人，房间里都有我。</em>}],
['You (Candidate)', q{The switch moment: during the ERP migration I wrote the requirements for the automated reconciliation module — <strong>48 pages, and it is still in production four years later.</strong> Somewhere in page 20 I realised I liked the requirements more than the month-end close. <em>That is not a mid-life crisis; that is a pattern with four years of evidence.</em>}, q{转折时刻：ERP 迁移中，我为自动对账模块写了需求——<strong>48 页，四年后仍在生产环境运行。</strong>大约在第 20 页时我意识到，比起月末结账，我更喜欢写需求。<em>这不是中年危机；这是有四年证据的模式。</em>}],
['Sarah (Hiring Manager)', q{Fair. <em>What transfers, and what do you need to learn?</em>}, q{合理。<em>什么能迁移过来，什么需要补？</em>}],
['You (Candidate)', q{<strong>Transfers on day one:</strong> finance domain depth — I have done the close, the reconciliations, the audit trail; your finance systems team will never have to explain what a suspense account is to me. <strong>Also transfers:</strong> control thinking — accountants are trained to assume everything can go wrong, <em>which is 80% of writing acceptance criteria</em>.}, q{<strong>第一天就能用的：</strong>财务领域深度——结账、对账、审计链路我都做过；你们的财务系统团队永远不需要向我解释什么是暂记科目。<strong>同样能用的：</strong>控制思维——会计受的训练就是假设一切都会出错，<em>而这就是验收标准写作的 80%</em>。}],
['You (Candidate)', q{<strong>What I need to learn:</strong> the tooling layer — Jira hygiene at bank scale, Confluence templates, your BRD standards. <em>That is a one-quarter learning curve, not a career risk</em> — and I would rather name it precisely than pretend it away.}, q{<strong>需要补的：</strong>工具层——银行规模的 Jira 规范、Confluence 模板、你们的 BRD 标准。<em>这是一个季度的学习曲线，不是职业风险</em>——我宁愿精确地说出它，也不假装它不存在。}],
['Sarah (Hiring Manager)', q{And the "sticks" part? <em>What stops you drifting back to accounting in two years?</em>}, q{那"不会转回去"的部分呢？<em>什么能阻止你两年后又飘回会计？</em>}],
['You (Candidate)', q{Two structural answers, not promises. <strong>One:</strong> the market — finance-transformation BA roles pay and grow faster than accounting at my level; the drift is against my own interest. <strong>Two:</strong> the evidence — I have already made the move inside my last company and stayed three years. <em>People do not revert to what they were good at; they revert to what was expected of them.</em> Nobody expects me to hold a ledger anymore.}, q{两个结构性答案，不是承诺。<strong>一：</strong>市场——我这个级别，财务变革类 BA 岗位的薪酬和成长都快于会计；"飘回去"违背我自己的利益。<strong>二：</strong>证据——我在上一家公司内部已经完成过这次转身，并持续了三年。<em>人不会退回到自己擅长的领域；人只会退回到被期待的领域。</em>已经没有人期待我记账了。}],
['Sarah (Hiring Manager)', q{You have answered my objection before I finished raising it. Let\'s talk about the team.}, q{我还没把疑虑问完，你已经把它答完了。我们来聊聊团队吧。}],
],
phrases => [
