['You (Candidate)', q{Surprisingly, a PM lesson: <strong>caring for someone full-time is stakeholder management with no authority and no off-hours</strong> — coordinating doctors, insurers, siblings. I came back with a sharper instinct for <em>what people need to hear versus what they need decided</em>. <strong>I would not recommend the tuition fees, but the course was real.</strong>}, q{意外的是一个 PM 层面的收获：<strong>全职照护是一场没有职权、没有下班的利益相关方管理</strong>——协调医生、保险、兄弟姐妹。我回来后对<em>"人们需要听到什么 vs 需要被决定什么"</em>的直觉更锋利了。<strong>学费不推荐，课程是真的。</strong>}],
