grammar => [
['Past perfect for before-the-gap, past simple for during', q{<em>"My father had surgery and I was the one on the ground."</em> — the past perfect (had surgery) quietly places the event before your care period; past simple carries the during. Gap answers are timeline exercises: <em>"By the time I re-entered, I had already finished the certification."</em> — one had-done re-anchors the whole sequence.}, q{"My father had surgery and I was the one on the ground."——过去完成时（had surgery）悄悄把事件定位在照护期之前；一般过去时承载期间。空窗回答就是时间线练习："By the time I re-entered, I had already finished the certification."——一句 had done 重排整个时间序列。}],
['Comparatives with sized clocks', q{<em>"Weeks, not months."</em>, <em>"Two weeks to rebuild, and it is a stronger habit now."</em> — gap answers win on sized comparatives: [duration], not [duration]. The grammar forces you to pick a number, and numbers are what convert worry into plan. "Stronger now than before the break" is the comparative that ends the decay story.}, q{"Weeks, not months."、"Two weeks to rebuild, and it is a stronger habit now."——空窗回答靠带刻度的比较句取胜：[时长]，不是[时长]。这种语法逼你给出数字，而数字把担忧变成计划。"Stronger now than before the break" 是终结"退化叙事"的那个比较句。}],
],
tips => [
q{<strong>Match the procedural tone.</strong> Grace is doing her job; answer in kind. Emotional defence invites emotional probing.},
q{<strong>Conviction once, then logistics.</strong> "I would make the same choice again" — say it once and move to the maintenance log. Repeating it reads as seeking forgiveness.},
q{<strong>The maintenance log is the answer.</strong> Certification, open source, portfolio — absence is only a problem when it is the whole story.},
q{<strong>Map your rust honestly.</strong> Current / rusty / gone — three buckets, sized in weeks. Panels trust candidates who audit themselves.},
q{<strong>Harvest the lesson.</strong> Full-time care as stakeholder management is a real, transferable read — one sentence, then back to the present.},
],
