['Passive for protocol, active for action', q{<em>"The pipeline snapshots the state file"</em> (active — your system acts) versus <em>"the change record lists both approvers"</em> (present simple — protocol states). Cross-region English leans on the passive for rules — <em>"approvals are kept local"</em> — and on the active for your own steps. Mixing them correctly tells the room you know the difference between how the system behaves and what you do.}, q{"The pipeline snapshots the state file"（主动——你的系统在做事）对 "the change record lists both approvers"（一般现在时——规程陈述）。跨区域英语用被动讲规则——"approvals are kept local"——用主动讲自己的步骤。混用得当，全场都能听出你分得清"系统的行为"与"你的动作"。}],
],
