dialogue => [
['Sarah (Hiring Manager)', q{Your CV says three years contracting. <em>Why permanent now — and if we offered a contract extension instead, would you take it?</em>}, q{简历上写着三年合同工。<em>为什么现在想转长期——如果我们给合同延期，你会接受吗？</em>}],
['You (Candidate)', q{Two honest answers, and they connect. <strong>Why permanent:</strong> my optimisation function changed. Years one and two, I optimised for <em>rate and variety</em> — three industries in eighteen months taught me more than any single employer could. <strong>What I optimise for now is scope and consequence</strong> — owning a domain long enough to see my decisions age. Contracts rarely give you that.}, q{两个诚实的回答，而且相互关联。<strong>为什么转长期：</strong>我的最优函数变了。头两年我最大化的是<em>费率和多样性</em>——18 个月里三个行业，比任何单一雇主教得都多。<strong>现在我最大化的是空间和后果</strong>——长期拥有一个领域，看着自己的决定随时间发酵。合同很少给你这个。}],
['You (Candidate)', q{<strong>Would I take the extension?</strong> If it were offered first and permanent became possible later — yes, without drama; I have done two renewals and left both cleanly. <strong>But I would not want the extension to become the plan</strong> — my answer today is that I am structuring my next three years around ownership, and I would rather that be explicit on both sides.}, q{<strong>会接受延期吗？</strong>如果先有延期、长期后置——会，不带戏剧性；我续过两次约，两次都干净退场。<strong>但我不想让延期变成默认计划</strong>——我今天的回答是：我的下一个三年是围绕"拥有"来构建的，这一点我希望双方都明确。}],
['Sarah (Hiring Manager)', q{That is clear. <em>Contractors sometimes get frozen out of the culture — team meetings, strategy days. How do you handle being on the outside of the permanent circle?</em>}, q{很清楚。<em>合同工有时会被排除在文化之外——团队会议、战略日。你怎么面对"长期圈子之外"的位置？</em>}],
['You (Candidate)', q{By being precise about the boundary instead of resenting it. <strong>I attend what affects my delivery</strong> — standups, planning, incident reviews. <strong>I do not expect</strong> comp committees or org design offsites, and I do not ask. <em>The boundary is real; the professionalism is choosing not to poll it.</em> In my last engagement I ran the team\'s incident process for eleven months — the permanent engineers briefed me into everything that mattered. <strong>Inclusion follows delivery, not employment status.</strong>}, q{我的方式是把边界说清楚，而不是心怀怨气。<strong>影响我交付的我参加</strong>——站会、计划会、事故复盘。<strong>我不期待</strong>薪酬委员会或组织设计外出会，也不去问。<em>边界是真实的；职业化在于选择不去试探它。</em>上一个项目里我主持了团队 11 个月的事故流程——正式员工把所有重要的事都同步给了我。<strong>融入跟随交付，而不是雇佣身份。</strong>}],
['Sarah (Hiring Manager)', q{Last angle: <em>if we hire you permanent and a hot market doubles contractor rates next year — will you be back on the market?</em>}, q{最后一个角度：<em>如果我们给你长期合同，明年市场火热、合同工费率翻倍——你会回到市场吗？</em>}],
['You (Candidate)', q{You should ask that question — and the honest answer has the same shape as the first one: <strong>I priced the market for three years; I know exactly what it pays.</strong> I am choosing permanent at a known discount because scope is what I am buying. <em>If I ever re-enter the market, you will hear it from me first, in a handover plan — not from a competitor\'s invoice.</em>}, q{这个问题应该问——诚实的答案和第一个答案同构：<strong>我为市场定过三年价，我很清楚它付多少。</strong>我在已知折价的情况下选择长期，因为我买的是空间。<em>如果有一天我重回市场，你会第一个从我这里听到——带着交接计划，而不是从竞争对手的账单上。</em>}],
['Sarah (Hiring Manager)', q{That is the most honest answer to that question I have heard this year. Welcome aboard — pending the usual process.}, q{这是今年我对这个问题听到的最诚实的回答。欢迎加入——走完常规流程即可。}],
],
phrases => [
['Function', q{My optimisation function changed.}, q{我的最优函数变了。}, q{Borrowed from engineering, perfect for this question: name what you maximise, and when it changed.}],
['Then/Now', q{Years one and two, I optimised for rate and variety. Now, scope and consequence.}, q{头两年我要费率和多样性；现在要空间和后果。}, q{The then/now frame makes change sound like strategy, not drift.}],
['Renewal', q{I have done two renewals and left both cleanly.}, q{我续过两次约，两次都干净退场。}, q{Contractor evidence that answers the loyalty question better than any promise.}],
['Boundary', q{The boundary is real; the professionalism is choosing not to poll it.}, q{边界是真实的；职业化在于选择不去试探它。}, q{How contractors talk about culture exclusion without resentment — and how permanent staff should hear it.}],
['Inclusion', q{Inclusion follows delivery, not employment status.}, q{融入跟随交付，而不是雇佣身份。}, q{The maxim that reframes the whole contractor-culture question.}],
['Guarantee', q{You will hear it from me first, in a handover plan.}, q{你会第一个从我这里听到——带着交接计划。}, q{The only credible answer to "will you leave": not a promise of forever, a protocol of exit.}],
],
vocab => [
['Contractor', 'n. 合同工', 'Engaged for a fixed term via an agency or own company; paid for scope, not tenure.'],
['Permanent', 'n. 长期雇员', 'Direct employment with benefits, notice periods and tenure.'],
['Rate', 'n. 费率', 'The contractor\'s day rate — typically higher, with no paid leave.'],
['Renewal / extension', 'n. 续约/延期', 'Extending a contract term; the contractor\'s version of a performance review.'],
['Optimisation function', 'n. 最优函数', 'What you are maximising — rate, learning, stability, or scope.'],
['Comp committee', 'n. 薪酬委员会', 'Where permanent salaries are decided — firmly outside contractor scope.'],
['Handover plan', 'n. 交接计划', 'The documented exit — the professional\'s answer to leaving.'],
['Notice period', 'n. 通知期', 'Permanent employees give one; contractors give whatever the contract says.'],
['Day rate', 'n. 日费率', 'Contractor pricing unit — compare with permanent pay carefully, not naively.'],
],
grammar => [
['Past simple for the old function, present for the new', q{<em>"Years one and two, I optimised for rate and variety."</em> — past simple, closed chapter. <em>"What I optimise for now is scope and consequence."</em> — present simple with a <strong>what</strong>-cleft, putting the new function on stage. The tense system is the argument: change is real, the present is chosen. Career-direction answers live in this past-to-present grammar.}, q{"Years one and two, I optimised for rate and variety."——过去时，已完结的章节。"What I optimise for now is scope and consequence."——现在时 + <strong>what</strong> 分裂句，把新的最优函数请上台。时态系统就是论点：改变是真的，现在是选择的。职业方向类回答都活在这种"过去到现在"的语法里。}],
['Protocols instead of promises', q{<em>"You will hear it from me first, in a handover plan."</em> — notice the grammar of the answer: not "I will never leave" (a promise about feelings) but a <strong>protocol sentence</strong> — who gets told, in what form, first. Protocols are checkable; promises are vibes. When an interviewer asks about loyalty, upgrade the answer from promise to protocol.}, q{"You will hear it from me first, in a handover plan."——注意答案的语法：不是"我永远不会走"（关于情绪的承诺），而是一句<strong>协议式陈述</strong>——谁先被告知、以什么形式。协议可核验；承诺只是氛围。当面试官问忠诚度时，把答案从承诺升级为协议。}],
],
tips => [
q{<strong>Name your optimisation function.</strong> Rate, variety, stability, scope — pick honestly and date the change. The then/now frame turns three years of contracting into a strategy.},
q{<strong>Renewals are your loyalty evidence.</strong> Two clean renewals and two clean exits answer the "will you stay" question better than any vow.},
q{<strong>Do not poll the boundary.</strong> Attend what affects delivery; skip what does not. Resentment at excluded meetings is a career tax you choose.},
q{<strong>"Inclusion follows delivery" is the line to live by.</strong> It is also the line panels quote to each other.},
q{<strong>Answer the leaving question with a protocol.</strong> A handover plan promised in advance is worth more than forever promised in the moment.},
],
practice => [
{ t => 'Your function, dated', p => 'Write your optimisation function — what you maximise now, what you maximised before, and the year it changed. Two sentences.', a => q{If the two functions are identical, that is an answer too — but say why it suits you: "I optimise for stability and depth; contracting was never my game." The error is drifting into an interview without knowing what you are maximising.} },
{ t => 'Boundary rehearsal', p => 'You are offered a contractor seat that excludes strategy days but includes incident command. Write your two-sentence boundary statement.', a => q{Model: "I attend everything that touches my delivery — including incident command, where I expect the same authority as anyone holding the pager. Strategy days are outside my scope and outside my interest." Authority attached to responsibility, boundaries stated without apology.} },
{ t => 'Protocol, not promise', p => 'Rewrite "I will definitely stay for three years" as a protocol sentence a hiring manager can actually rely on.', a => q{Model: "If either side misprices this in six months, you will hear it from me first — with a handover plan and a notice period, not a resignation email on a Friday." Honesty with structure beats enthusiasm with no exit plan.} },
],
},
]
